# Stages core.ts runs and files under src that no system tree describes yet.
#
# check-atlas.sh requires every stage and every source file to be either cited in a tree or listed
# here, so the atlas cannot quietly fall behind the pipeline: a NEW stage or file fails the build
# until somebody decides which system it belongs to. A line here is an admission, not an exemption.
#
# The gate also checks this file both ways (2026-09-04): an entry naming a file that no longer
# exists fails, and an entry naming a file a tree already cites fails — the first is how seven
# deleted files stayed listed for a day, the second how `engine/credit-price.ts` was both "unmapped"
# and cited by three trees. The list only shrinks, and the gate is what makes that true.
#
# Each entry is one of three things, and the next pass must say which:
#   · INFRASTRUCTURE a tree legitimately does not describe (columns/, workers, kernels, shims,
#     formatters, the UI shell) — these want an "OUT OF SCOPE, and why" line rather than a tree;
#   · a stage whose system IS mapped but whose file the mapping never needed to cite;
#   · a real gap — code doing something no required tree accounts for, which is the most
#     interesting kind of entry in this file and the reason it is not simply deleted.
